                <pb facs="0251" n="149" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg149"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10388/21.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister
                    Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-03-12"><hi rendition="#italic">March 12,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Root refers to department’s telegraphic instruction of June 8, 1906, and
                    instructs Mr. Rockhill to inform the Chinese Government that since the British
                    and German subjects have been paid for losses incurred in the Shanghai riots of
                    December, 1905, this Government, after careful investigation of the claims of
                    American citizens for losses suffered, has determined upon the sum of $889.73
                    gold in final settlement. Mr. Root directs that a formal demand for this amount
                    be presented.)</p>
            </div>
